1
00:00:47,652 --> 00:00:51,072
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:53,658 --> 00:00:57,579
<i>There's going to be a bus stop</i>
<i>about 300 meters in front of you.</i>

3
00:00:57,662 --> 00:00:59,080
<i>Do you see it?</i>

4
00:00:59,164 --> 00:01:00,248
Yes, I see it.

5
00:01:00,331 --> 00:01:02,041
Crash into the woman

6
00:01:02,125 --> 00:01:03,918
standing there!

7
00:01:12,802 --> 00:01:14,721
Please help my sister.

8
00:01:15,388 --> 00:01:16,598
What do you mean?

9
00:01:20,351 --> 00:01:21,311
My sister

10
00:01:21,936 --> 00:01:23,021
is Kang Ha-jeong.

11
00:01:23,104 --> 00:01:25,773
Kang Ha-jeong? The accounting manager?

12
00:01:30,069 --> 00:01:30,904
I think…

13
00:01:33,072 --> 00:01:34,699
she did something she shouldn't have.

14
00:01:35,533 --> 00:01:36,784
What do you mean?

15
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:38,786
She has a ledger.

16
00:01:39,412 --> 00:01:42,081
A ledger recording how
the apartment funds were embezzled.

17
00:01:45,501 --> 00:01:47,211
<i>Kang Ha-jeong, the accounting manager,</i>

18
00:01:47,795 --> 00:01:48,922
is Kang Ha-ri's sister.

19
00:01:49,005 --> 00:01:50,256
What?

20
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:54,219
And she has the actual ledger recording
how the reserve fund was embezzled.

21
00:01:54,302 --> 00:01:55,428
The ledger?

22
00:01:55,511 --> 00:01:56,846
The actual ledger?

23
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:59,098
Wasn't she working for Lee Chung-won?

24
00:02:00,350 --> 00:02:02,727
Lee Chung-won
doesn't seem to know about it either.

25
00:02:02,810 --> 00:02:06,356
Ms. Kang probably made it
to protect herself.

26
00:02:07,273 --> 00:02:09,359
Boss, doesn't this mean we have

27
00:02:09,442 --> 00:02:11,236
-a weapon against him now?
-Right.

28
00:02:11,319 --> 00:02:13,112
Only if we get our hands on it.

29
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:17,533
You guys keep an eye
on Kang Ha-jeong for now.

30
00:02:17,617 --> 00:02:18,493
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

31
00:02:18,576 --> 00:02:21,412
This could be a matter
of life and death for us.

32
00:02:21,496 --> 00:02:23,248
I'm telling you, I can't do this.

33
00:02:23,331 --> 00:02:25,917
I'm going to pretend I didn't hear this.

34
00:02:44,018 --> 00:02:47,814
She sat in the third row
from the back of the 125 bus.

35
00:02:56,114 --> 00:02:58,116
Yes, she's entering her house.

36
00:03:01,744 --> 00:03:03,913
<i>What is it? Did you get caught?</i>

37
00:03:03,997 --> 00:03:05,081
No, it's nothing.

38
00:03:05,832 --> 00:03:07,959
Ten billion for just driving?

39
00:03:08,042 --> 00:03:10,962
Boss, he's definitely planning
to take someone out.

40
00:03:11,045 --> 00:03:12,463
You can't do this, Boss.

41
00:03:12,547 --> 00:03:13,965
Boss, I'll do it instead.

42
00:03:14,048 --> 00:03:15,508
I've been the youngest for years.

43
00:03:15,591 --> 00:03:17,510
I have to be a better driver than you.

44
00:03:17,593 --> 00:03:20,346
The "hangnail" Lee Chung-won mentioned
must be Kang Ha-jeong.

45
00:03:23,599 --> 00:03:25,601
Will he stop if I refuse, though?

46
00:03:26,728 --> 00:03:29,147
He'll just get someone
desperate for money to do it instead.

47
00:03:30,148 --> 00:03:31,441
I need to take the wheel

48
00:03:31,524 --> 00:03:34,110
to get a chance to save Ms. Kang.

49
00:03:43,911 --> 00:03:46,122
Ms. Kang, are you okay?

50
00:03:46,205 --> 00:03:47,165
We're here to help.

51
00:04:11,314 --> 00:04:12,440
This is ten billion won.

52
00:04:13,232 --> 00:04:15,985
I told you I'd give you the money
once you did this.

53
00:04:16,611 --> 00:04:19,113
You can save your old boss
with this money.

54
00:04:19,197 --> 00:04:22,075
You shouldn't leave him there
when he's already sick.

55
00:04:22,658 --> 00:04:24,660
All you had to do

56
00:04:24,744 --> 00:04:26,788
was crash into a woman
standing right there.

57
00:04:26,871 --> 00:04:28,831
You've pulled off harder things than that,

58
00:04:28,915 --> 00:04:31,959
but you fail to do the easiest job?

59
00:04:33,211 --> 00:04:34,504
I may be a bad guy,

60
00:04:35,588 --> 00:04:37,298
but you're just trash.

61
00:04:38,633 --> 00:04:39,884
Trash?

62
00:04:40,885 --> 00:04:43,721
You're being quite rude to a guy
who's interested in you.

63
00:04:43,805 --> 00:04:45,473
I don't date trash.

64
00:04:45,556 --> 00:04:47,475
Then what will you do with me?

65
00:04:48,351 --> 00:04:50,520
I have an item that will interest you.

66
00:04:50,603 --> 00:04:52,480
A ledger of all the trashy things

67
00:04:52,563 --> 00:04:55,983
a construction company president did
to embezzle the reserve fund

68
00:04:56,067 --> 00:04:58,611
of an apartment complex
that he built himself.

69
00:05:05,618 --> 00:05:06,869
Then what about this?

70
00:05:08,121 --> 00:05:10,206
Let's exchange the ledger

71
00:05:11,207 --> 00:05:12,291
for Park Yong-man.

72
00:05:13,751 --> 00:05:15,086
You needed that ten billion

73
00:05:15,169 --> 00:05:18,256
to get Park Yong-man released.

74
00:05:18,339 --> 00:05:19,340
So…

75
00:05:25,346 --> 00:05:27,140
COMMISSIONER KWAK JU-GWON

76
00:05:33,563 --> 00:05:34,772
<i>Yes, Mr. Lee.</i>

77
00:05:34,856 --> 00:05:36,482
<i>What prompts this late-night call?</i>

78
00:05:36,566 --> 00:05:39,986
Commissioner, I have a favor to ask you.

79
00:05:40,611 --> 00:05:41,612
Let's get ready

80
00:05:41,696 --> 00:05:43,698
to release Park Yong-man on medical bail.

81
00:05:43,781 --> 00:05:46,826
<i>What? Park Yong-man?</i>

82
00:05:46,909 --> 00:05:49,120
The boss of Park Hae-kang,
the guy you've been using.

83
00:05:49,829 --> 00:05:52,456
I'll let you join the One Club,

84
00:05:53,958 --> 00:05:56,335
so get ready to release Park Yong-man.

85
00:05:57,003 --> 00:05:58,754
<i>All right. I'll get it ready.</i>

86
00:06:02,842 --> 00:06:04,468
If you want him released,

87
00:06:04,552 --> 00:06:07,096
bring me the ledger.

88
00:06:08,681 --> 00:06:09,515
Simple, isn't it?

89
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:21,652
My sister really isn't a bad person.

90
00:06:22,361 --> 00:06:23,446
I swear.

91
00:06:24,822 --> 00:06:26,199
<i>They say it's pancreatic cancer.</i>

92
00:06:27,325 --> 00:06:28,910
<i>He has about three months left.</i>

93
00:06:35,625 --> 00:06:38,669
I searched everywhere,
but the ledger isn't here.

94
00:06:38,753 --> 00:06:41,172
It seems she's already moved it.

95
00:06:41,255 --> 00:06:42,548
<i>It's not there?</i>

96
00:06:43,132 --> 00:06:45,509
Then that means
it's no longer just a document.

97
00:06:46,469 --> 00:06:48,137
It's a weapon now.

98
00:06:48,971 --> 00:06:51,390
I'm sorry, sir. I'll track her again.

99
00:06:52,058 --> 00:06:54,101
She can't hide forever.

100
00:06:55,311 --> 00:06:56,896
Good work, Mr. Kim.

101
00:07:00,691 --> 00:07:02,568
He really is competent.

102
00:07:03,194 --> 00:07:06,364
But if he keeps being unpredictable,

103
00:07:08,032 --> 00:07:09,533
it's going to be a problem.

104
00:07:11,369 --> 00:07:13,454
If I turn my back on him…

105
00:07:15,706 --> 00:07:18,251
he won't be able to handle it.

106
00:07:21,128 --> 00:07:25,841
THE APARTMENT JOB

107
00:07:38,771 --> 00:07:40,815
Ha-jeong!

108
00:07:42,316 --> 00:07:44,443
Ha-jeong, are you okay? Are you hurt?

109
00:07:44,527 --> 00:07:46,696
I can't believe this!

110
00:07:46,779 --> 00:07:48,364
Tell me.

111
00:07:48,447 --> 00:07:50,449
What bastard was trying to kill you?

112
00:07:50,533 --> 00:07:52,868
Tell me. You must know who it is!

113
00:07:57,873 --> 00:08:00,084
Who is it? Who did this to my sister?

114
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:03,462
Where's the ledger?

115
00:08:04,380 --> 00:08:06,132
You almost got killed because of it.

116
00:08:08,217 --> 00:08:09,969
I hid the ledger.

117
00:08:10,052 --> 00:08:11,554
She doesn't know where it is.

118
00:08:16,601 --> 00:08:18,352
Give me the ledger.

119
00:08:18,936 --> 00:08:20,688
It's not something you can handle.

120
00:08:22,189 --> 00:08:25,067
And why would you need to take
something that dangerous?

121
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:26,902
I need it

122
00:08:26,986 --> 00:08:28,738
to at least try to make a deal.

123
00:08:28,821 --> 00:08:29,905
A deal?

124
00:08:30,531 --> 00:08:31,490
With who?

125
00:08:31,574 --> 00:08:33,242
The person who tried to kill my sister?

126
00:08:33,743 --> 00:08:34,577
Who is it?

127
00:08:35,202 --> 00:08:37,121
The former president?
Or the facility manager?

128
00:08:37,204 --> 00:08:38,956
Who is it?

129
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,127
If they want to kill my sister over it,

130
00:08:43,210 --> 00:08:45,212
then that means the ledger
is their weakness.

131
00:08:45,296 --> 00:08:47,840
So why should I hand it over to you?

132
00:08:48,716 --> 00:08:49,675
Mr. Park.

133
00:08:50,551 --> 00:08:53,012
That ledger is also
a record of my sister's crimes.

134
00:08:53,554 --> 00:08:55,139
I can't just hand it over.

135
00:08:55,222 --> 00:08:56,724
The person after her life

136
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,769
isn't someone you can handle.

137
00:08:59,852 --> 00:09:02,021
You're not even telling me
who this person is.

138
00:09:02,104 --> 00:09:03,814
How can I trust you with the ledger?

139
00:09:04,690 --> 00:09:06,400
That ledger is my sister's lifeline.

140
00:09:07,068 --> 00:09:08,986
Her life depends on it right now.

141
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:09,987
I can't hand it over.

142
00:09:16,452 --> 00:09:17,370
So you mean

143
00:09:17,453 --> 00:09:20,456
the accounting manager
is Kang Ha-ri's sister?

144
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:23,876
That means she's working
with the penthouse guy.

145
00:09:26,712 --> 00:09:29,423
How did our enemy end up

146
00:09:29,507 --> 00:09:32,134
sitting right in the middle
of our living room?

147
00:09:32,218 --> 00:09:34,720
Hang on. It's going to be tough

148
00:09:34,804 --> 00:09:38,683
having to make meals
for Ms. Kang and her sister too.

149
00:09:39,850 --> 00:09:42,353
There's another mouth to feed now.

150
00:09:42,436 --> 00:09:44,063
Well, this is an emergency.

151
00:09:44,814 --> 00:09:47,400
We just have to set the table
for one more person, right?

152
00:09:47,483 --> 00:09:49,985
Fine. You don't have to be so serious.

153
00:09:51,278 --> 00:09:54,615
I hope she's not a glutton
like somebody here.

154
00:09:59,328 --> 00:10:00,871
Where are you going, Gyeong-buk?

155
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:03,708
Here.

156
00:10:03,791 --> 00:10:04,959
Kang Ha-ri said

157
00:10:05,042 --> 00:10:07,962
sweets are the best for stress.

158
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:13,592
CHOCOLATE MILK

159
00:10:19,390 --> 00:10:20,307
Thanks.

160
00:10:22,101 --> 00:10:23,227
So she likes chocolate.

161
00:10:23,769 --> 00:10:25,062
Shameless.

162
00:10:25,896 --> 00:10:27,565
She does seem to like food.

163
00:10:27,648 --> 00:10:31,235
We got the security cam footage
near Kang Ha-jeong's last known location.

164
00:10:32,194 --> 00:10:35,364
She was last seen entering
True Value's Building 114.

165
00:10:36,365 --> 00:10:38,826
Building 114?
That's where Park Hae-kang lives.

166
00:10:38,909 --> 00:10:39,910
Yes, sir.

167
00:10:40,494 --> 00:10:42,747
We assume she's in his house.

168
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:44,582
What? Are they dating?

169
00:10:45,166 --> 00:10:47,293
Kang Ha-jeong has a little sister

170
00:10:47,376 --> 00:10:48,794
named Kang Ha-ri.

171
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,921
She's Park Hae-kang's wife.

172
00:10:52,089 --> 00:10:54,133
What's going on here?

173
00:10:54,216 --> 00:10:57,303
So they're in-laws?

174
00:10:57,386 --> 00:10:58,888
It's actually more complicated.

175
00:10:58,971 --> 00:11:02,683
Park Hae-kang and Kang Ha-ri
aren't registered as spouses.

176
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:05,519
His so-called brothers
are men from his gambling den,

177
00:11:05,603 --> 00:11:07,438
and his father is actually
a wanted gambler.

178
00:11:08,063 --> 00:11:10,816
His entire family is fake.

179
00:11:11,942 --> 00:11:12,777
What?

180
00:11:14,904 --> 00:11:17,323
Wow. You've got to be kidding me.

181
00:11:18,741 --> 00:11:20,326
How ridiculous.

182
00:11:21,202 --> 00:11:22,661
What about his wife?

183
00:11:22,745 --> 00:11:26,415
She was hired through a stand-in service
to play the role of his bride.

184
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:31,712
So this whole thing was just

185
00:11:32,213 --> 00:11:33,964
a business arrangement between them?

186
00:11:34,548 --> 00:11:36,467
Just a business arrangement.

187
00:11:38,219 --> 00:11:40,221
That means they'll come
wagging their tails

188
00:11:41,722 --> 00:11:43,724
at the smell of money.

189
00:11:44,558 --> 00:11:45,768
How easy.

190
00:11:51,565 --> 00:11:53,901
I hid the ledger in a safe spot.

191
00:11:55,319 --> 00:11:56,904
No one will be able to find it.

192
00:12:00,032 --> 00:12:00,908
I'm sorry.

193
00:12:01,992 --> 00:12:04,119
I didn't expect things to get this bad.

194
00:12:06,247 --> 00:12:07,164
Who is it?

195
00:12:07,998 --> 00:12:09,583
Who ordered you to embezzle the fund?

196
00:12:11,001 --> 00:12:11,835
It was me.

197
00:12:13,212 --> 00:12:14,630
I made the choice.

198
00:12:15,297 --> 00:12:16,799
Nobody ordered me to do it.

199
00:12:19,426 --> 00:12:20,261
So it's me.

200
00:12:21,679 --> 00:12:22,930
I'm the one who ordered it.

201
00:12:24,014 --> 00:12:25,808
You needed the money to support me.

202
00:12:26,809 --> 00:12:27,643
Ha-ri.

203
00:12:29,436 --> 00:12:30,563
I was so scared

204
00:12:31,689 --> 00:12:33,107
that something would happen to you.

205
00:12:36,443 --> 00:12:37,278
I'm sorry.

206
00:12:38,112 --> 00:12:39,321
I'm sorry, Ha-ri.

207
00:12:43,284 --> 00:12:46,287
Why won't she give it to you
when things have gotten so bad?

208
00:12:46,370 --> 00:12:49,665
I really didn't expect her to be so cold.

209
00:12:49,748 --> 00:12:50,791
It's understandable.

210
00:12:50,874 --> 00:12:53,502
Her sister's life is on the line.
She won't just hand it over.

211
00:12:53,586 --> 00:12:55,045
Hey, whose side are you on?

212
00:12:55,838 --> 00:12:58,215
Whose side? We're all family here.

213
00:12:58,299 --> 00:12:59,508
Don't be stupid. Boss.

214
00:13:00,342 --> 00:13:01,176
What do we do now?

215
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:02,928
Ms. Kang is right.

216
00:13:03,804 --> 00:13:05,389
Asking her for the ledger

217
00:13:05,472 --> 00:13:08,100
is the same as sacrificing
Kang Ha-jeong for our sake.

218
00:13:08,183 --> 00:13:10,060
Then what about Yong-man?

219
00:13:10,144 --> 00:13:11,812
Without the ledger, how would we--

220
00:13:11,895 --> 00:13:13,439
That's why we're going with Plan B.

221
00:13:13,522 --> 00:13:15,399
We're going after Lee Chung-won
without the ledger.

222
00:13:15,482 --> 00:13:16,650
Lee Chung-won?

223
00:13:18,485 --> 00:13:21,530
Boss, we'd be fighting against Taesan.

224
00:13:21,614 --> 00:13:23,699
We don't even have
any leverage against them.

225
00:13:23,782 --> 00:13:24,908
I'll make that myself.

226
00:13:25,659 --> 00:13:28,412
But have you guys heard of the One Club?

227
00:13:28,495 --> 00:13:29,413
One Club?

228
00:13:29,496 --> 00:13:30,664
No, I've never been there.

229
00:13:31,248 --> 00:13:32,333
The one in Hongdae?

230
00:13:34,752 --> 00:13:36,754
<i>I'll let you join the One Club,</i>

231
00:13:37,546 --> 00:13:39,632
so get ready to release Park Yong-man.

232
00:13:40,424 --> 00:13:42,676
The commissioner was behind
Chief Son Dae-un.

233
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:45,220
The commissioner needed ten billion won

234
00:13:45,304 --> 00:13:46,930
to join this "One Club,"

235
00:13:47,014 --> 00:13:48,682
and that's why
Mr. Son demanded it from us.

236
00:13:48,766 --> 00:13:49,725
What?

237
00:13:52,603 --> 00:13:55,606
What kind of big shots
are in this One Club

238
00:13:55,689 --> 00:13:57,232
that you need ten billion to join?

239
00:13:57,858 --> 00:13:58,901
Right?

240
00:13:59,443 --> 00:14:00,527
It seems like

241
00:14:01,362 --> 00:14:03,447
Lee Chung-won is managing that club.

242
00:14:04,406 --> 00:14:06,992
Let's dig into what kind of people
are in this One Club

243
00:14:07,076 --> 00:14:10,037
and what Lee Chung-won is trying

244
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,538
to pull there.

245
00:14:11,622 --> 00:14:12,456
Yes, Boss.

246
00:14:13,374 --> 00:14:14,833
She's not picking up?

247
00:14:15,417 --> 00:14:16,877
No. Her phone's off.

248
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:19,421
She's not the type to skip work like this.

249
00:14:19,505 --> 00:14:20,756
I wonder what's going on.

250
00:14:22,174 --> 00:14:23,384
Let's focus on work for now.

251
00:14:24,218 --> 00:14:25,135
I'm sure she'll call.

252
00:14:26,261 --> 00:14:27,179
Try calling her again.

253
00:14:27,262 --> 00:14:28,222
-Should I?
-Yes.

254
00:14:30,724 --> 00:14:33,477
<i>Ha-jeong, are you all right?</i>

255
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:34,395
<i>Say something.</i>

256
00:14:35,187 --> 00:14:36,438
<i>You're scaring me.</i>

257
00:14:37,731 --> 00:14:39,775
Good morning, everyone!

258
00:14:39,858 --> 00:14:40,985
-Hello.
-Good morning.

259
00:14:41,068 --> 00:14:42,861
What brings you here so early?

260
00:14:43,529 --> 00:14:47,408
This is my workplace.
Of course, I should be here.

261
00:14:47,491 --> 00:14:49,243
-Isn't that right?
-Yes, of course.

262
00:14:51,245 --> 00:14:52,371
Mr. Choi.

263
00:14:52,454 --> 00:14:55,874
Please call a meeting
with the tenant representatives.

264
00:14:55,958 --> 00:14:58,460
What? The tenant representatives?

265
00:14:59,378 --> 00:15:01,714
Why do you need…

266
00:15:01,797 --> 00:15:05,592
I'm the president.
I can't sit back and do nothing.

267
00:15:05,676 --> 00:15:08,762
It's my duty to work for this apartment.

268
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:13,767
Please call a tenants' representative
meeting immediately.

269
00:15:19,523 --> 00:15:22,067
Mom, your eyes are red.

270
00:15:23,235 --> 00:15:25,112
Did you have a fight with your sister?

271
00:15:25,738 --> 00:15:28,240
No, we just stayed up late chatting.

272
00:15:29,241 --> 00:15:32,369
She looked like
she had a nightmare, though.

273
00:15:34,663 --> 00:15:37,583
I wish Ha-jeong would keep
staying with us.

274
00:15:38,083 --> 00:15:39,084
Why?

275
00:15:39,168 --> 00:15:41,587
Uncle Hae-kang
and my dad will protect her.

276
00:15:42,504 --> 00:15:44,465
Then she won't be scared anymore.

277
00:15:51,138 --> 00:15:52,306
But Mom.

278
00:15:54,975 --> 00:15:57,186
There's a worm
growing in our kindergarten wall.

279
00:15:57,978 --> 00:16:00,022
It keeps getting longer.

280
00:16:00,105 --> 00:16:01,732
I'm scared it'll turn into a snake.

281
00:16:03,233 --> 00:16:04,818
A worm is getting longer?

282
00:16:05,944 --> 00:16:08,030
My teacher told me it's a secret.

283
00:16:08,572 --> 00:16:10,574
So don't tell anyone about it.

284
00:16:18,290 --> 00:16:19,458
-Hello.
-Good morning.

285
00:16:19,541 --> 00:16:21,335
-Hello.
-See you later, Gyeong-buk.

286
00:16:21,418 --> 00:16:22,252
-Okay.
-Bye.

287
00:16:22,336 --> 00:16:23,462
Bye.

288
00:16:26,757 --> 00:16:28,175
-Hello.
-Hello.

289
00:16:28,801 --> 00:16:31,011
Would you like to join us for coffee?

290
00:16:31,804 --> 00:16:32,930
Coffee?

291
00:16:36,016 --> 00:16:39,061
You know Su-a, who transferred
to the Harvard Class yesterday?

292
00:16:39,144 --> 00:16:39,978
I met her mom,

293
00:16:40,062 --> 00:16:42,397
and she said
Su-a got a rash all over her body

294
00:16:42,481 --> 00:16:44,983
as soon as she started
going to kindergarten.

295
00:16:45,067 --> 00:16:46,985
She asked if Seo-jun was okay.

296
00:16:47,069 --> 00:16:51,240
Ru-i actually developed eczema
while attending kindergarten too,

297
00:16:51,323 --> 00:16:54,576
but we couldn't be sure
it was because of that.

298
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:58,038
You know how we'd suspected
they had used cheap materials?

299
00:16:58,122 --> 00:16:59,748
-Yeah.
-Right.

300
00:16:59,832 --> 00:17:01,166
And Hye-jun told me

301
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:03,085
she used an umbrella in class yesterday,

302
00:17:03,168 --> 00:17:05,254
so I first thought
they were just having fun.

303
00:17:05,337 --> 00:17:07,172
But she said water fell from the ceiling.

304
00:17:07,256 --> 00:17:08,257
Goodness.

305
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:10,551
Min-jun said it was raining in class too.

306
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:13,637
What if it really was shoddy construction?

307
00:17:14,346 --> 00:17:16,765
There's a worm
growing in our kindergarten wall.

308
00:17:17,349 --> 00:17:19,017
It keeps getting longer.

309
00:17:19,643 --> 00:17:21,812
We filed a complaint
with the Office of Education,

310
00:17:21,895 --> 00:17:23,605
-but they said it's fine.
-Right.

311
00:17:23,689 --> 00:17:26,024
A private inspection company came
and checked everything.

312
00:17:26,108 --> 00:17:26,942
They said it's safe.

313
00:17:27,025 --> 00:17:29,611
Well, it's the law.
What else can we do anyway?

314
00:17:30,237 --> 00:17:31,822
It's not the law.

315
00:17:31,905 --> 00:17:33,240
The method was wrong.

316
00:17:33,991 --> 00:17:37,161
Don't trust the kindergarten.
File an information disclosure request.

317
00:17:37,244 --> 00:17:39,621
We should compare each item
on the diagnostic report.

318
00:17:39,705 --> 00:17:41,373
We can view the report?

319
00:17:42,082 --> 00:17:43,167
It's our right as citizens.

320
00:17:43,876 --> 00:17:46,170
This should be reported
as a public interest violation.

321
00:17:46,795 --> 00:17:49,381
Children's safety
is a matter of public interest.

322
00:17:49,464 --> 00:17:50,465
If we report this

323
00:17:50,549 --> 00:17:53,051
to the Civil Rights Commission,
the officials will have to act.

324
00:17:54,553 --> 00:17:57,014
You're so smart, Ms. Kang.

325
00:17:57,097 --> 00:17:59,349
How do you know stuff like that?

326
00:18:00,392 --> 00:18:02,603
I just know a tiny bit.

327
00:18:03,353 --> 00:18:07,399
Then you can come with us
to the Office of Education.

328
00:18:07,983 --> 00:18:08,817
She's right.

329
00:18:08,901 --> 00:18:10,027
-That's a great idea.
-Yes.

330
00:18:10,652 --> 00:18:11,486
Me?

331
00:18:11,570 --> 00:18:13,363
-Let's go together.
-Right.

332
00:18:13,447 --> 00:18:14,948
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

333
00:18:15,532 --> 00:18:16,825
I'm so glad.

334
00:18:18,869 --> 00:18:21,455
Why did I have to say that?

335
00:18:21,538 --> 00:18:22,956
I'm not even a lawyer.

336
00:18:23,457 --> 00:18:25,834
You should stop meddling
in other people's lives.

337
00:18:25,918 --> 00:18:28,212
Just worry about yourself and Ha-jeong.

338
00:18:30,297 --> 00:18:32,341
President Park's wife?

339
00:18:37,179 --> 00:18:38,722
Yes, that's me.

340
00:18:39,556 --> 00:18:40,390
Who…

341
00:18:44,102 --> 00:18:48,315
I'm just curious how much you know
about your husband.

342
00:18:51,735 --> 00:18:54,529
Should I call you Kang Ha-jeong's sister?

343
00:18:59,201 --> 00:19:01,161
UNDER REPAIR
WILL BE COMPLETED SOON

344
00:19:02,162 --> 00:19:03,830
Here, Kang Ha-ri.

345
00:19:06,291 --> 00:19:09,169
Your sister did something quite bold.

346
00:19:11,588 --> 00:19:12,881
So it's you.

347
00:19:13,966 --> 00:19:15,467
You tried to kill my sister.

348
00:19:16,051 --> 00:19:17,511
You're quick-witted.

349
00:19:17,594 --> 00:19:19,471
You're right. That was me.

350
00:19:20,973 --> 00:19:22,140
You bastard.

351
00:19:22,808 --> 00:19:26,019
You're smart, but you're naive.

352
00:19:27,354 --> 00:19:29,106
Am I the only bad guy here?

353
00:19:29,189 --> 00:19:31,441
Is your sister a good person, then?

354
00:19:32,526 --> 00:19:34,361
Your sister teamed up with a bad guy

355
00:19:34,444 --> 00:19:37,906
and helped him cover up his crimes.

356
00:19:42,703 --> 00:19:44,705
How about 500 million?

357
00:19:44,788 --> 00:19:47,749
Your sister's severance pay and bonus.

358
00:19:47,833 --> 00:19:50,502
But I want that ledger in return.

359
00:19:54,172 --> 00:19:55,299
Why not?

360
00:19:55,382 --> 00:19:58,969
I'm sure that's more than what you got
for playing Park Hae-kang's wife.

361
00:20:07,394 --> 00:20:09,563
The pay is better,
but the benefits aren't that great.

362
00:20:10,856 --> 00:20:13,025
How can I trust a boss
who tried to kill someone

363
00:20:13,108 --> 00:20:14,568
who worked for him?

364
00:20:15,944 --> 00:20:17,529
So you're the type to hold grudges.

365
00:20:17,612 --> 00:20:19,031
Forget it.

366
00:20:21,116 --> 00:20:22,617
If you touch my sister again,

367
00:20:24,077 --> 00:20:26,538
I'll make you realize you messed

368
00:20:26,621 --> 00:20:28,248
with the wrong person.

369
00:20:28,957 --> 00:20:30,959
Your sister is staying
at Park Hae-kang's, right?

370
00:20:31,668 --> 00:20:35,630
Do you really think Park Hae-kang
will protect you two until the end?

371
00:20:37,591 --> 00:20:39,885
At least he doesn't
stab people in the back.

372
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:44,264
You really have no clue, do you?

373
00:20:46,308 --> 00:20:49,019
Park Hae-kang actually came here

374
00:20:49,895 --> 00:20:52,981
to take the 17 billion won
in the reserve fund.

375
00:20:56,193 --> 00:20:58,945
He can only take the fund
if he's the president.

376
00:20:59,613 --> 00:21:01,740
He's been using you.

377
00:21:02,949 --> 00:21:04,242
Do you still not get it?

378
00:21:09,873 --> 00:21:11,166
Gyeong-buk.

379
00:21:13,335 --> 00:21:14,169
Hang on.

380
00:21:17,714 --> 00:21:18,882
Candied sweet potatoes.

381
00:21:21,676 --> 00:21:22,594
Are you dreaming?

382
00:21:23,095 --> 00:21:24,096
Move.

383
00:21:26,056 --> 00:21:26,890
You were right.

384
00:21:28,809 --> 00:21:30,852
I was bored just sitting around.

385
00:21:30,936 --> 00:21:33,897
There were some sweet potatoes,
so I made a snack for Gyeong-buk.

386
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:35,690
I made plenty, so have some.

387
00:21:36,566 --> 00:21:38,110
I didn't know you had such talent.

388
00:21:40,445 --> 00:21:42,948
Come and have some. They're tasty.

389
00:22:01,925 --> 00:22:03,218
Your gaze

390
00:22:03,301 --> 00:22:05,971
is sweeter
than the candied sweet potatoes.

391
00:22:09,182 --> 00:22:10,600
Come and try this.

392
00:22:10,684 --> 00:22:12,144
-Come on.
-Come here.

393
00:22:12,227 --> 00:22:13,145
Try some.

394
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:16,231
-Enjoy.
-Thank you.

395
00:22:16,314 --> 00:22:17,482
You're welcome.

396
00:22:20,068 --> 00:22:20,944
Mr. Park.

397
00:22:22,988 --> 00:22:24,114
Where's Park Hae-kang?

398
00:22:24,698 --> 00:22:25,866
Come out here!

399
00:22:25,949 --> 00:22:27,742
Ha-ri, what's wrong?

400
00:22:30,996 --> 00:22:31,997
What?

401
00:22:33,206 --> 00:22:35,542
-What is it?
-Is it true?

402
00:22:35,625 --> 00:22:36,459
Is what true?

403
00:22:37,127 --> 00:22:39,504
The reason why you were
desperate to become the president.

404
00:22:42,215 --> 00:22:43,091
Was it all

405
00:22:44,467 --> 00:22:46,344
because of the 17 billion
in the reserve fund?

406
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:58,982
Did you meet Lee Chung-won?

407
00:23:01,443 --> 00:23:02,277
Yes.

408
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:04,404
I could tell when I met him.

409
00:23:05,822 --> 00:23:07,699
That man is openly evil,

410
00:23:07,782 --> 00:23:10,160
but you're a real fraud
who pretends to be a good guy

411
00:23:10,243 --> 00:23:12,078
-while stabbing people in the back.
-Ms. Kang.

412
00:23:12,162 --> 00:23:13,788
You're being too harsh…

413
00:23:18,543 --> 00:23:19,920
So?

414
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:24,633
Do you feel betrayed because I'm a fraud?

415
00:23:25,842 --> 00:23:26,760
Ms. Kang,

416
00:23:27,636 --> 00:23:29,596
stop pretending like you're a victim.

417
00:23:32,098 --> 00:23:32,933
What?

418
00:23:33,016 --> 00:23:35,477
You pretended to be my wife
because you needed money too.

419
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:36,811
Method acting?

420
00:23:37,562 --> 00:23:38,521
Paid labor?

421
00:23:39,105 --> 00:23:40,190
Don't be silly.

422
00:23:40,273 --> 00:23:44,236
You chose to be part of a fake family
because of money.

423
00:23:49,866 --> 00:23:50,825
You're right.

424
00:23:51,409 --> 00:23:52,786
I did this for the money.

425
00:23:52,869 --> 00:23:54,579
But at the very least,

426
00:23:55,413 --> 00:23:58,792
I never betrayed people's trust
while pretending to be righteous.

427
00:23:59,501 --> 00:24:02,379
I thought you were sincerely
trying to make this a better place.

428
00:24:03,171 --> 00:24:04,172
I just feel

429
00:24:05,298 --> 00:24:08,635
so embarrassed
that I took your side because of that.

430
00:24:11,846 --> 00:24:12,681
Ha-jeong.

431
00:24:13,682 --> 00:24:15,600
Let's go. I can't stay here any longer.

432
00:24:18,103 --> 00:24:19,396
What will you do once you leave?

433
00:24:21,773 --> 00:24:23,525
Why do you think
Lee Chung-won met with you?

434
00:24:25,402 --> 00:24:26,278
This means

435
00:24:26,945 --> 00:24:28,405
he knows where Ha-jeong is.

436
00:24:30,282 --> 00:24:32,784
Let's talk inside for a moment.

437
00:24:46,673 --> 00:24:47,757
Park Hae-kang

438
00:24:48,967 --> 00:24:51,177
saved me when I almost died.

439
00:24:52,137 --> 00:24:53,805
I know that,

440
00:24:53,888 --> 00:24:56,474
but he's also the one
who planned all this to take the fund.

441
00:24:57,142 --> 00:25:00,729
You did this because of money too.
Why do you expect him to be innocent?

442
00:25:06,526 --> 00:25:10,280
He saved me when he knew
that 17 billion was already gone.

443
00:25:11,406 --> 00:25:14,576
You keeping the ledger hidden
isn't helping him in any way,

444
00:25:14,659 --> 00:25:16,077
but look.

445
00:25:16,161 --> 00:25:19,039
He's putting himself at risk
by protecting us.

446
00:25:23,918 --> 00:25:25,128
You may be used to

447
00:25:26,546 --> 00:25:31,426
being called a fraud and a thug
by other people,

448
00:25:31,509 --> 00:25:34,888
but it must be the first time
hearing it from someone who trusted you.

449
00:25:36,973 --> 00:25:39,434
That's why you have
that look on your face.

450
00:25:40,685 --> 00:25:42,020
What look?

451
00:25:44,647 --> 00:25:46,524
You look like you got caught being human

452
00:25:47,108 --> 00:25:49,319
despite being a fraud.

453
00:25:54,282 --> 00:25:56,576
Let's begin True Value State's first

454
00:25:56,659 --> 00:25:59,496
tenants' representative council meeting.

455
00:26:00,747 --> 00:26:04,042
Welcome, everyone.

456
00:26:05,585 --> 00:26:09,589
We did name this
a tenants' council meeting,

457
00:26:09,672 --> 00:26:11,049
but our real goal

458
00:26:11,132 --> 00:26:13,510
is for everyone to get along here,

459
00:26:13,593 --> 00:26:17,347
regardless of whether
the unit is a rental or owner-occupied.

460
00:26:18,473 --> 00:26:21,851
Everything you say is absolutely right.

461
00:26:23,436 --> 00:26:25,688
Do you have any ideas, President Jang?

462
00:26:25,772 --> 00:26:26,606
I would like

463
00:26:27,482 --> 00:26:31,152
to suggest a safety patrol.

464
00:26:31,778 --> 00:26:35,615
But President Jang,
we already have guards…

465
00:26:37,409 --> 00:26:41,621
Before arguing about
who the true owners of True Value are,

466
00:26:41,704 --> 00:26:43,540
we should show everyone

467
00:26:43,623 --> 00:26:46,543
that we're the ones

468
00:26:46,626 --> 00:26:50,171
who care the most about this place.

469
00:26:50,922 --> 00:26:52,090
So,

470
00:26:52,173 --> 00:26:53,800
starting tonight,

471
00:26:53,883 --> 00:26:56,719
who wants to join me
in patrolling the complex?

472
00:27:02,183 --> 00:27:03,852
Right. Thank you.

473
00:27:05,228 --> 00:27:06,855
I knew it.

474
00:27:08,523 --> 00:27:10,942
We elected such good representatives.

475
00:27:11,609 --> 00:27:13,903
Cats never come this way.

476
00:27:13,987 --> 00:27:15,238
They always stay over there.

477
00:27:16,281 --> 00:27:17,740
Gosh. Look.

478
00:27:18,408 --> 00:27:19,409
The light's off.

479
00:27:19,492 --> 00:27:21,494
The trail in front of Building 107.

480
00:27:21,578 --> 00:27:22,871
-Write that down.
-Okay.

481
00:27:22,954 --> 00:27:23,955
Okay.

482
00:27:24,038 --> 00:27:25,498
Shall we go that way?

483
00:27:26,332 --> 00:27:27,292
Excuse me.

484
00:27:28,251 --> 00:27:30,253
-Where do you live?
-Building 109.

485
00:27:30,336 --> 00:27:31,588
This building?

486
00:27:31,671 --> 00:27:33,548
We're True Value's safety patrol.

487
00:27:33,631 --> 00:27:36,468
The building reps are working hard
for this apartment complex.

488
00:27:37,635 --> 00:27:39,262
-This building?
-Yes.

489
00:27:39,345 --> 00:27:41,723
-You shouldn't stay out too late.
-Okay.

490
00:27:41,806 --> 00:27:43,266
-It's a dangerous world.
-Right.

491
00:27:43,349 --> 00:27:44,309
You can't see me.

492
00:27:44,392 --> 00:27:45,685
No, you hold it.

493
00:27:46,811 --> 00:27:48,563
Stretch your arm out, okay?

494
00:27:49,397 --> 00:27:50,398
Kids!

495
00:27:51,566 --> 00:27:53,318
What are you doing?

496
00:27:53,401 --> 00:27:55,904
It's late, you know.

497
00:27:56,946 --> 00:27:58,948
Hyeong-u, don't you live in Building 105?

498
00:27:59,032 --> 00:28:00,825
Yes. Hello.

499
00:28:00,909 --> 00:28:02,785
Your mom will be waiting. Go home.

500
00:28:02,869 --> 00:28:04,704
How many girlfriends do you have?

501
00:28:04,787 --> 00:28:05,872
Gosh!

502
00:28:06,414 --> 00:28:07,248
I'll call you!

503
00:28:07,332 --> 00:28:08,458
-Don't.
-Okay.

504
00:28:08,541 --> 00:28:10,043
Stop making your mom worry!

505
00:28:10,126 --> 00:28:12,504
Everyone knows
he gives his mom a hard time.

506
00:28:12,587 --> 00:28:14,088
He's too handsome for his own good.

507
00:28:14,672 --> 00:28:16,591
Great work today, everyone.

508
00:28:16,674 --> 00:28:18,343
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

509
00:28:18,426 --> 00:28:19,886
-I'll see you tomorrow.
-All right.

510
00:28:19,969 --> 00:28:22,096
I'm going to take a detour back home.

511
00:28:22,180 --> 00:28:23,848
-Okay.
-Bye.

512
00:28:23,932 --> 00:28:25,391
-Bye.
-Bye.

513
00:28:25,475 --> 00:28:26,809
-Bye.
-Bye.

514
00:28:26,893 --> 00:28:29,521
TRUE VALUE KINDERGARTEN

515
00:28:39,989 --> 00:28:41,115
What is that?

516
00:28:52,460 --> 00:28:53,711
What is all this?

517
00:28:54,337 --> 00:28:55,296
Goodness.

518
00:28:55,797 --> 00:28:57,173
It's going to crumble down soon.

519
00:28:57,841 --> 00:28:59,133
My gosh.

520
00:29:07,684 --> 00:29:08,560
You scared me.

521
00:29:09,269 --> 00:29:11,312
What are you doing?

522
00:29:16,818 --> 00:29:18,695
Why do I feel so thirsty?

523
00:29:22,574 --> 00:29:23,533
Do you remember

524
00:29:24,117 --> 00:29:27,704
how you said it feels
like you have to repay your sister?

525
00:29:30,290 --> 00:29:31,583
What about it?

526
00:29:32,250 --> 00:29:33,877
I told you I have someone like that too.

527
00:29:35,295 --> 00:29:36,129
So?

528
00:29:37,672 --> 00:29:38,548
That person

529
00:29:39,507 --> 00:29:41,092
is in jail right now.

530
00:29:42,051 --> 00:29:43,177
And he's innocent.

531
00:29:43,678 --> 00:29:47,223
For people like me,
there are only two ways

532
00:29:47,307 --> 00:29:49,058
to get involved with the police.

533
00:29:50,059 --> 00:29:51,895
Greasing their palms
and coexisting with them,

534
00:29:52,645 --> 00:29:54,439
or getting hauled in as a suspect.

535
00:29:58,401 --> 00:29:59,819
I did the former.

536
00:30:00,612 --> 00:30:03,364
I was one of their favorite cash cows.

537
00:30:04,908 --> 00:30:08,161
But the ones who thought of me
as a goose laying golden eggs

538
00:30:08,244 --> 00:30:11,372
took my old boss to cut me open.

539
00:30:12,165 --> 00:30:14,000
And they told me to bring ten billion

540
00:30:15,418 --> 00:30:17,003
if I wanted to get him released.

541
00:30:18,838 --> 00:30:23,259
That's when I found out
there was money in this apartment complex.

542
00:30:24,469 --> 00:30:26,888
I did all this
because of the reserve fund.

543
00:30:27,472 --> 00:30:29,933
It's true I became the president
with ill intentions.

544
00:30:30,016 --> 00:30:33,269
And it's true that I dragged you into this

545
00:30:33,353 --> 00:30:35,104
when you had no clue.

546
00:30:37,190 --> 00:30:39,859
I just thought it would be better
for you not to know,

547
00:30:40,902 --> 00:30:41,778
but I guess

548
00:30:43,404 --> 00:30:44,656
I've only deceived you.

549
00:30:48,660 --> 00:30:49,661
I apologize.

550
00:30:51,788 --> 00:30:52,789
I'm sorry.

551
00:30:58,294 --> 00:30:59,545
So what will you do now?

552
00:31:00,797 --> 00:31:04,217
There's no money in the account,
and I won't give you the ledger.

553
00:31:05,551 --> 00:31:07,261
I'll find another way.

554
00:31:08,346 --> 00:31:09,430
Even so,

555
00:31:10,264 --> 00:31:13,559
I promise to keep the two of you safe.

556
00:31:19,399 --> 00:31:21,109
I promise.

557
00:31:25,446 --> 00:31:27,532
Have it with a poached egg.

558
00:31:27,615 --> 00:31:28,741
This isn't cheese?

559
00:31:28,825 --> 00:31:29,867
All right.

560
00:31:31,411 --> 00:31:33,705
Here. Enjoy.

561
00:31:34,288 --> 00:31:35,832
Asparagus?

562
00:31:38,918 --> 00:31:39,752
Gyeong-buk.

563
00:31:40,420 --> 00:31:42,463
Tell Ha-ri to eat.

564
00:31:43,214 --> 00:31:46,217
Ha-ri, Uncle Hae-kang said you should eat.

565
00:31:46,884 --> 00:31:50,179
Gyeong-buk, tell your uncle
that I don't have an appetite.

566
00:31:52,098 --> 00:31:53,808
She doesn't have an appetite?

567
00:31:53,891 --> 00:31:56,686
She'll have no energy all day
if she skips breakfast.

568
00:31:56,769 --> 00:31:58,646
Tell her to at least have a bite.

569
00:32:00,189 --> 00:32:01,816
Tell him to stay out of my business

570
00:32:01,899 --> 00:32:04,360
and enjoy his own meal.

571
00:32:08,656 --> 00:32:10,158
My teacher said

572
00:32:10,241 --> 00:32:12,160
fighting is bad,

573
00:32:12,243 --> 00:32:15,204
and not making up after that
is even worse.

574
00:32:15,288 --> 00:32:16,539
You're awful.

575
00:32:17,498 --> 00:32:19,292
Gyeong-buk, we're not fighting--

576
00:32:19,375 --> 00:32:20,251
Just make up.

577
00:32:21,002 --> 00:32:23,629
If you don't,
I'm not going to kindergarten today.

578
00:32:23,713 --> 00:32:24,672
I'm not eating, either!

579
00:32:25,506 --> 00:32:27,717
-Good job, Gyeong-buk!
-Nice!

580
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:28,760
Gyeong-buk's angry.

581
00:32:28,843 --> 00:32:30,219
Fine, let's make up.

582
00:32:30,303 --> 00:32:31,804
Okay. Let's make up.

583
00:32:31,888 --> 00:32:34,015
Gyeong-buk, we made up.

584
00:32:34,098 --> 00:32:35,975
-We made up.
-We made up.

585
00:32:36,059 --> 00:32:37,143
Now hug each other.

586
00:32:37,643 --> 00:32:39,062
-What?
-What?

587
00:32:39,145 --> 00:32:42,398
My teacher said you have to hug
when you apologize.

588
00:32:42,482 --> 00:32:45,109
No, there's no need.

589
00:32:46,069 --> 00:32:48,571
Gyeong-buk's teacher is very wise.

590
00:32:49,822 --> 00:32:52,617
Come on. We should apologize too.

591
00:32:52,700 --> 00:32:53,701
Let's make up.

592
00:32:53,785 --> 00:32:55,203
-We should apologize.
-What?

593
00:32:55,286 --> 00:32:56,329
-What…
-Let's make up.

594
00:32:56,412 --> 00:32:57,622
No, it's fine.

595
00:32:57,705 --> 00:32:58,831
Let's go.

596
00:32:58,915 --> 00:33:00,541
-I said it's fine!
-They need to hug?

597
00:33:00,625 --> 00:33:02,001
What are you doing?

598
00:33:02,877 --> 00:33:04,712
Okay, fine. Let's make up.

599
00:33:04,796 --> 00:33:06,297
We're making up.

600
00:33:06,380 --> 00:33:07,673
-Let's make up.
-Bigger hug!

601
00:33:08,341 --> 00:33:09,592
-Bigger hug!
-Bigger hug!

602
00:33:16,140 --> 00:33:18,935
TRUE VALUE KINDERGARTEN
ENROLLMENT OPEN

603
00:33:23,564 --> 00:33:25,483
What do I do?

604
00:33:28,027 --> 00:33:29,195
If I expose this,

605
00:33:29,278 --> 00:33:31,405
I'll become a traitor to True Value.

606
00:33:33,241 --> 00:33:35,159
Bye!

607
00:33:36,536 --> 00:33:37,703
Mom!

608
00:33:42,959 --> 00:33:45,378
Gosh. This is giving me a headache.

609
00:33:45,461 --> 00:33:46,796
Oh dear.

610
00:33:50,967 --> 00:33:54,303
Construction will officially start
next month.

611
00:33:55,388 --> 00:33:56,764
I wanted you to see the empty plot

612
00:33:58,141 --> 00:33:59,684
before that.

613
00:33:59,767 --> 00:34:02,436
Everything here will change completely.

614
00:34:02,520 --> 00:34:04,772
You should see this place one last time.

615
00:34:05,523 --> 00:34:08,526
I hope you'll care about the project
as it takes shape

616
00:34:08,609 --> 00:34:11,487
and show lots of support.

617
00:34:11,571 --> 00:34:14,031
You know my son-in-law's
law firm represents

618
00:34:15,324 --> 00:34:17,201
the top legal figures in Korea, right?

619
00:34:17,285 --> 00:34:18,119
Yes.

620
00:34:18,202 --> 00:34:21,497
So proceed with the project
without worrying about legal issues.

621
00:34:21,581 --> 00:34:23,207
Speed is the most important.

622
00:34:23,291 --> 00:34:26,586
The relic incident slowed things down.
Let's speed things up.

623
00:34:26,669 --> 00:34:29,881
Of course. I'll have everything
moving so fast, it'll be hard to keep up.

624
00:34:29,964 --> 00:34:31,632
We're going to start releasing articles.

625
00:34:31,716 --> 00:34:33,634
I'll get the prices up.

626
00:34:34,343 --> 00:34:36,554
The VIP is keeping an eye on this as well.

627
00:34:37,305 --> 00:34:40,057
Oman New Town is emerging
as a potential solution

628
00:34:40,766 --> 00:34:44,520
to the housing shortage in Seoul!

629
00:34:46,939 --> 00:34:48,858
We'll provide
all the policy support you need.

630
00:34:48,941 --> 00:34:50,026
Thank you.

631
00:34:51,152 --> 00:34:52,403
Thank you, everyone!

632
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:55,615
OMAN NEW TOWN
GEOLOGICAL SURVEY

633
00:34:55,698 --> 00:34:57,491
Let's zoom in.

634
00:34:58,159 --> 00:35:00,036
I can even see their pores.

635
00:35:00,119 --> 00:35:01,746
This camera is amazing.

636
00:35:01,829 --> 00:35:03,331
Can you tell who they are?

637
00:35:05,750 --> 00:35:06,626
That guy…

638
00:35:07,251 --> 00:35:09,128
I saw him on the news.

639
00:35:09,212 --> 00:35:12,089
Who was he again?
He's always with the president.

640
00:35:12,173 --> 00:35:13,966
The Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs.

641
00:35:14,050 --> 00:35:15,885
And the president of <i>Gongyeong Daily.</i>

642
00:35:15,968 --> 00:35:18,179
They're all gathered
to fill their pockets.

643
00:35:18,262 --> 00:35:20,181
My fingers are trembling.

644
00:35:20,264 --> 00:35:21,974
Get their faces clearly.

645
00:35:23,184 --> 00:35:25,436
These will be their memorial photos.

646
00:35:32,735 --> 00:35:34,320
You're not allowed to take photos here.

647
00:35:34,403 --> 00:35:36,781
-Sorry about that.
-Move your equipment.

648
00:35:37,740 --> 00:35:40,159
We had to conduct a geological survey.

649
00:35:40,243 --> 00:35:43,454
We're just here to do our job. Look!

650
00:35:43,537 --> 00:35:44,497
We're heading out.

651
00:35:44,580 --> 00:35:45,915
We'll wrap up now!

652
00:35:45,998 --> 00:35:47,458
We're almost done.

653
00:35:47,541 --> 00:35:49,418
ONE CLUB

654
00:35:49,502 --> 00:35:50,670
Look, Boss.

655
00:35:51,254 --> 00:35:53,422
Construction, law,

656
00:35:53,506 --> 00:35:54,674
politics,

657
00:35:55,299 --> 00:35:56,384
media.

658
00:35:56,467 --> 00:35:58,636
Korea's most powerful figures
are all gathered here.

659
00:36:01,389 --> 00:36:03,140
Can you recognize this man?

660
00:36:03,975 --> 00:36:05,643
The Senior Secretary for Civil Affairs.

661
00:36:05,726 --> 00:36:07,728
The official right below the president.

662
00:36:07,812 --> 00:36:10,398
And next to him
is the Supreme Court Justice.

663
00:36:10,481 --> 00:36:11,649
And in the back

664
00:36:11,732 --> 00:36:15,111
are the president of <i>Gongyeong Daily</i>
and the Prosecutor General.

665
00:36:16,404 --> 00:36:18,781
They're the members of the One Club.

666
00:36:19,532 --> 00:36:21,617
No wonder he wasn't scared of anything.

667
00:36:21,701 --> 00:36:24,370
He was using
the entire country as his shield.

668
00:36:29,667 --> 00:36:31,085
I didn't order any food.

669
00:36:32,003 --> 00:36:33,254
Ms. Kang.

670
00:36:34,797 --> 00:36:37,341
What is it? I was sleeping…

671
00:36:39,135 --> 00:36:40,303
Look at this.

672
00:36:44,348 --> 00:36:45,766
What is this?

673
00:36:45,850 --> 00:36:48,311
That's Gyeong-buk's kindergarten.

674
00:36:49,478 --> 00:36:53,149
That's what the exterior wall
looks like right now.

675
00:36:53,232 --> 00:36:54,942
But we can see the rebar.

676
00:36:55,026 --> 00:36:57,486
Couldn't the building
collapse at any moment?

677
00:36:57,570 --> 00:37:00,656
The kindergarten mothers
suspected shoddy construction too.

678
00:37:00,740 --> 00:37:04,577
I've been so torn about what to do.

679
00:37:04,660 --> 00:37:07,204
If I expose this issue,

680
00:37:07,288 --> 00:37:09,290
the apartment prices will drop for sure,

681
00:37:09,373 --> 00:37:12,376
and they'll attack the rental units again,

682
00:37:12,460 --> 00:37:14,462
saying we don't care if the prices drop.

683
00:37:15,546 --> 00:37:17,882
Still, this isn't a trivial matter.

684
00:37:21,093 --> 00:37:21,927
President Park,

685
00:37:22,845 --> 00:37:25,514
I think you should step up
and handle this.

686
00:37:28,100 --> 00:37:28,976
All right.

687
00:37:29,518 --> 00:37:31,771
This involves the safety of the kids here.

688
00:37:31,854 --> 00:37:33,647
Of course,
I should step up as the president.

689
00:37:35,816 --> 00:37:37,443
TRUE VALUE KINDERGARTEN

690
00:37:42,073 --> 00:37:43,282
Wait just a moment.

691
00:37:45,534 --> 00:37:47,078
Are you filming a prison escape movie?

692
00:37:47,161 --> 00:37:49,288
<i>Papillon</i> really ruined all you kids.

693
00:37:54,585 --> 00:37:56,128
Are you filming a spy movie or what?

694
00:37:56,212 --> 00:37:58,339
Tom Cruise really ruined all you kids.

695
00:37:59,131 --> 00:38:00,091
This isn't mine.

696
00:38:00,174 --> 00:38:01,384
That's mine.

697
00:38:01,467 --> 00:38:02,718
Everyone, move aside.

698
00:38:03,219 --> 00:38:04,428
Let me smash it in.

699
00:38:07,932 --> 00:38:08,849
Get a grip!

700
00:38:08,933 --> 00:38:12,353
It'll cost the residents money
to get it fixed if you break it.

701
00:38:13,187 --> 00:38:15,189
Ma Dong-seok ruined all you kids.

702
00:38:15,272 --> 00:38:16,148
Step back!

703
00:38:17,983 --> 00:38:18,943
Move aside.

704
00:38:25,199 --> 00:38:27,493
<i>Security has been disabled.</i>

705
00:38:28,828 --> 00:38:30,287
You had a key?

706
00:38:30,371 --> 00:38:33,207
-You should've told us.
-I told you.

707
00:38:33,958 --> 00:38:35,709
He's got main character syndrome.

708
00:38:40,923 --> 00:38:42,550
All right. Gosh.

709
00:38:46,011 --> 00:38:47,513
Check thoroughly.

710
00:38:49,890 --> 00:38:53,227
Cracks in the wall and stuff.

711
00:38:53,310 --> 00:38:55,062
Check if there's anything off.

712
00:38:55,938 --> 00:38:57,398
We'll check thoroughly.

713
00:39:06,740 --> 00:39:09,118
You idiot. Are you stealing kids' candy?

714
00:39:09,201 --> 00:39:11,036
Are you here to stuff your face?

715
00:39:51,911 --> 00:39:53,287
Worm.

716
00:39:53,370 --> 00:39:55,164
Right. The worm.

717
00:40:00,419 --> 00:40:01,545
What's that?

718
00:40:12,348 --> 00:40:14,683
Are you crying?

719
00:40:16,268 --> 00:40:17,770
No…

720
00:40:22,358 --> 00:40:23,651
It's leaking.

721
00:40:35,955 --> 00:40:37,248
Oh my gosh.

722
00:40:38,040 --> 00:40:40,167
It wasn't just one crack.

723
00:40:43,671 --> 00:40:45,798
Is this the spot you were talking about?

724
00:40:45,881 --> 00:40:46,882
Pull it back.

725
00:40:49,969 --> 00:40:51,637
You shouldn't see this, Mr. Kim.

726
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:52,972
-Why?
-Hey.

727
00:40:53,055 --> 00:40:54,932
-Stay calm.
-Let go.

728
00:40:59,019 --> 00:41:00,229
What is this?

729
00:41:02,022 --> 00:41:04,942
The mothers filed a complaint,
so an inspection company came,

730
00:41:05,025 --> 00:41:06,068
but they said it was safe.

731
00:41:06,652 --> 00:41:08,320
What part of this is safe?

732
00:41:08,404 --> 00:41:09,905
This is practically attempted murder.

733
00:41:09,989 --> 00:41:12,157
I can't believe these assholes.

734
00:41:12,241 --> 00:41:14,159
I guess Taesan really is powerful.

735
00:41:14,243 --> 00:41:16,453
How could they even
think about covering this up?

736
00:41:16,537 --> 00:41:18,998
That's why we need to figure out
what to do about this.

737
00:41:20,207 --> 00:41:21,584
What should we do, President Park?

738
00:41:29,049 --> 00:41:30,384
No. Never.

739
00:41:30,467 --> 00:41:32,553
You can't go to kindergarten today.

740
00:41:33,137 --> 00:41:33,971
Why not?

741
00:41:35,306 --> 00:41:37,766
Well, the kindergarten…

742
00:41:37,850 --> 00:41:38,934
-Just don't go.
-I…

743
00:41:39,018 --> 00:41:42,229
I also want you
to skip kindergarten today.

744
00:41:43,731 --> 00:41:45,649
Then who will I play with?

745
00:41:46,942 --> 00:41:49,069
We can all play with you.

746
00:41:50,529 --> 00:41:51,780
Why are you looking at me?

747
00:42:00,789 --> 00:42:03,709
Do you not care about the other kids?

748
00:42:03,792 --> 00:42:05,669
It's fine as long as your kid is safe?

749
00:42:06,253 --> 00:42:09,548
Turning a blind eye
makes you equally guilty, Mr. Park.

750
00:42:12,343 --> 00:42:14,094
All right. I'll let you

751
00:42:14,178 --> 00:42:15,929
play at a kids cafe today.

752
00:42:16,013 --> 00:42:17,556
And bring all your friends!

753
00:42:20,142 --> 00:42:21,769
You're the best!

754
00:42:22,394 --> 00:42:24,021
Why is he so excited?

755
00:42:24,813 --> 00:42:26,190
What's a kids cafe?

756
00:42:27,358 --> 00:42:29,943
It's like an indoor playground for kids

757
00:42:30,027 --> 00:42:32,071
and a battleground for parents.

758
00:42:57,346 --> 00:42:58,472
Wait!

759
00:42:58,555 --> 00:43:00,265
I'm afraid of heights.

760
00:43:13,404 --> 00:43:14,321
Why isn't it falling?

761
00:43:14,405 --> 00:43:15,823
Call the manager!

762
00:43:15,906 --> 00:43:17,574
Why do you need the manager?

763
00:43:24,039 --> 00:43:25,124
I got it!

764
00:43:25,207 --> 00:43:26,041
Good job!

765
00:43:26,125 --> 00:43:28,627
Bathroom! Where's the bathroom?

766
00:43:39,638 --> 00:43:40,472
I'm so exhausted.

767
00:43:40,556 --> 00:43:42,057
How are they so full of energy?

768
00:43:42,141 --> 00:43:44,059
Delivering packages was easier than this.

769
00:43:46,103 --> 00:43:47,396
Do you have pain relief patches?

770
00:43:47,479 --> 00:43:49,523
This counts as a workplace injury.

771
00:43:50,274 --> 00:43:54,445
Why do we keep spending money
when we're here to take it?

772
00:43:54,528 --> 00:43:56,739
Let's just leave, please.

773
00:43:56,822 --> 00:43:58,282
Just think of this as an investment.

774
00:44:03,120 --> 00:44:04,037
Boss!

775
00:44:05,247 --> 00:44:06,165
Boss!

776
00:44:30,939 --> 00:44:32,232
There's no movement, sir.

777
00:44:34,109 --> 00:44:36,111
Park Hae-kang isn't doing anything?

778
00:44:36,195 --> 00:44:37,029
No, sir.

779
00:44:38,071 --> 00:44:41,533
He's just walking
around the apartment complex

780
00:44:41,617 --> 00:44:42,868
and living quietly.

781
00:44:44,578 --> 00:44:46,705
He doesn't hate money,

782
00:44:47,414 --> 00:44:50,751
and he wouldn't just sit and watch
as his old boss dies.

783
00:44:53,462 --> 00:44:54,963
What's he up to?

784
00:44:55,589 --> 00:44:56,507
Mr. Kim.

785
00:44:57,174 --> 00:44:59,468
Did I overestimate Park Hae-kang?

786
00:45:00,677 --> 00:45:03,347
Should I keep watching him, sir?

787
00:45:06,475 --> 00:45:08,852
He'll have no choice but to come to me.

788
00:45:09,603 --> 00:45:13,065
That ledger will become useless
if Park Yong-man dies.

789
00:45:14,733 --> 00:45:15,567
You can go.

790
00:45:16,276 --> 00:45:17,110
Yes, sir.

791
00:45:38,632 --> 00:45:40,968
Even if you keep holding out
until the end,

792
00:45:42,636 --> 00:45:44,304
all that will be left

793
00:45:45,514 --> 00:45:47,933
is this single photo.

794
00:45:48,600 --> 00:45:49,977
You're such a fool,

795
00:45:50,978 --> 00:45:52,020
Park Hae-kang.

796
00:45:58,318 --> 00:46:00,487
I called for an urgent meeting today

797
00:46:01,154 --> 00:46:03,448
because something is happening
in True Value State

798
00:46:04,032 --> 00:46:06,743
that I simply cannot turn a blind eye to.

799
00:46:07,578 --> 00:46:08,745
President Jang.

800
00:46:08,829 --> 00:46:10,122
CONSTRUCTION DEFECTS

801
00:46:10,205 --> 00:46:11,373
What is that?

802
00:46:11,456 --> 00:46:12,666
What's that?

803
00:46:13,333 --> 00:46:14,710
Are those photos real?

804
00:46:14,793 --> 00:46:17,004
Is this why
the kindergarten was shut down?

805
00:46:17,087 --> 00:46:19,423
These are photos
from True Value's kindergarten.

806
00:46:19,506 --> 00:46:23,343
As you can see,
this goes beyond a minor defect.

807
00:46:23,969 --> 00:46:26,263
I had the kindergarten shut down
as the president.

808
00:46:26,346 --> 00:46:27,180
Hold on.

809
00:46:27,264 --> 00:46:30,100
Has the building really aged this fast?

810
00:46:30,183 --> 00:46:31,518
No,

811
00:46:31,602 --> 00:46:34,396
this is clearly a sign
of shoddy construction.

812
00:46:34,479 --> 00:46:36,315
-Shoddy construction?
-Shoddy construction?

813
00:46:38,900 --> 00:46:42,738
Do you know how serious an issue this is?

814
00:46:42,821 --> 00:46:45,240
This could make our property values
plummet overnight.

815
00:46:45,324 --> 00:46:46,533
That's not the problem!

816
00:46:46,617 --> 00:46:48,702
Don't you see the cracks in the photos?

817
00:46:49,411 --> 00:46:53,040
I trusted the director
and thought it was safe.

818
00:46:53,790 --> 00:46:57,169
The inspection company
stated that the kindergarten was safe

819
00:46:57,252 --> 00:47:01,006
because it was a subsidiary
of Taesan Construction.

820
00:47:05,260 --> 00:47:08,722
So they were putting our children
in danger the whole time?

821
00:47:09,973 --> 00:47:13,060
You're making a fuss
over something that hasn't happened yet.

822
00:47:13,143 --> 00:47:16,980
The president is being overly worried,
calling it shoddy construction.

823
00:47:17,064 --> 00:47:19,524
Let's not cause a commotion.

824
00:47:19,608 --> 00:47:21,610
This concerns the safety of our children.

825
00:47:21,693 --> 00:47:24,780
We must explain the situation
to the residents

826
00:47:24,863 --> 00:47:26,031
and make it public--

827
00:47:26,114 --> 00:47:27,324
Wait. Make it public?

828
00:47:27,407 --> 00:47:29,618
Can't we just get things repaired quietly?

829
00:47:29,701 --> 00:47:31,411
Repairs won't fix everything.

830
00:47:31,495 --> 00:47:34,748
We should file a complaint and demand
action from Taesan Construction.

831
00:47:34,831 --> 00:47:36,541
We can't send our kids back there.

832
00:47:37,167 --> 00:47:39,252
Then send them
to a different kindergarten.

833
00:47:39,336 --> 00:47:41,713
There are dozens of kindergartens
in our neighborhood.

834
00:47:41,797 --> 00:47:43,465
Right. Send them somewhere else.

835
00:47:43,548 --> 00:47:45,467
Imagine what will happen if rumors spread.

836
00:47:45,550 --> 00:47:47,594
Look, I got the chills
just thinking about it.

837
00:47:47,678 --> 00:47:49,137
I'm more scared about that.

838
00:47:49,221 --> 00:47:51,348
You should think
about the residents' assets.

839
00:47:51,431 --> 00:47:52,933
Their houses are everything to them.

840
00:47:53,016 --> 00:47:55,644
In any case,
this can never be made public.

841
00:47:56,812 --> 00:47:58,563
A president dropping apartment prices?

842
00:47:58,647 --> 00:48:00,023
Whose side are you even on?

843
00:48:00,524 --> 00:48:02,025
You should just step down!

844
00:48:02,109 --> 00:48:03,485
Yes, step down.

845
00:48:03,568 --> 00:48:04,569
Step down!

846
00:48:05,112 --> 00:48:07,239
Everyone, listen.

847
00:48:10,283 --> 00:48:13,787
You can't trade
our children's safety for money.

848
00:48:14,413 --> 00:48:16,957
And if an accident occurs
at the kindergarten,

849
00:48:17,040 --> 00:48:18,125
what would you do then?

850
00:48:18,208 --> 00:48:20,085
-You're just a tenant!
-You're just a tenant!

851
00:48:20,711 --> 00:48:22,170
The homeowners are speaking.

852
00:48:22,254 --> 00:48:24,131
You don't care
because it's not your own house.

853
00:48:24,214 --> 00:48:28,260
Property prices are a serious matter
directly tied to our livelihoods.

854
00:48:29,052 --> 00:48:30,554
Fine, I get it.

855
00:48:32,556 --> 00:48:34,224
Continue the meeting, President Park.

856
00:48:34,307 --> 00:48:35,142
Unbelievable.

857
00:48:41,857 --> 00:48:42,899
Just a moment.

858
00:48:45,152 --> 00:48:46,903
Who among you

859
00:48:46,987 --> 00:48:49,156
doesn't have any children?

860
00:48:49,239 --> 00:48:50,240
Raise your hands.

861
00:48:56,913 --> 00:48:57,914
All right, then.

862
00:48:58,457 --> 00:49:00,584
I will do my job as president.

863
00:49:00,667 --> 00:49:02,002
PRESIDENT PARK HAE-KANG

864
00:49:08,091 --> 00:49:08,925
Yes?

865
00:49:13,096 --> 00:49:14,389
What are you going to do?

866
00:49:16,808 --> 00:49:18,852
What will you do
about the defective construction?

867
00:49:18,935 --> 00:49:21,688
Are you going to drop it
just because they're opposing it?

868
00:49:21,772 --> 00:49:24,065
We should make a formal complaint…

869
00:49:24,149 --> 00:49:26,067
No, wait. Let's report this to the media.

870
00:49:26,651 --> 00:49:28,612
Lee Chung-won has control
over the media as well.

871
00:49:29,529 --> 00:49:31,656
So you're just going to sit back
and do nothing?

872
00:49:31,740 --> 00:49:34,701
If we can't use the media,
we can become the media instead.

873
00:49:42,793 --> 00:49:44,002
Ms. Kang is here too.

874
00:49:47,255 --> 00:49:48,381
Perfect timing, everyone.

875
00:49:48,465 --> 00:49:49,424
What?

876
00:49:51,885 --> 00:49:55,639
We came to tell you
we won't just transfer kindergartens.

877
00:49:55,722 --> 00:49:58,225
This isn't just
a minor construction mistake.

878
00:49:58,308 --> 00:50:00,602
They put our children's lives
at risk for money.

879
00:50:00,685 --> 00:50:02,562
We should ring the bell for society.

880
00:50:03,355 --> 00:50:04,481
You mean "sound the alarm."

881
00:50:05,065 --> 00:50:05,899
Right.

882
00:50:05,982 --> 00:50:08,527
Can you think of any ideas,
President Park?

883
00:50:15,742 --> 00:50:16,868
It's right here.

884
00:50:19,287 --> 00:50:20,121
Me?

885
00:50:22,082 --> 00:50:22,916
Why?

886
00:50:22,999 --> 00:50:24,417
DAMN IN-LAWS

887
00:50:27,796 --> 00:50:29,256
<i>Damn in-laws.</i>

888
00:50:29,339 --> 00:50:32,592
<i>Mother, only factories would make</i>

889
00:50:32,676 --> 00:50:35,303
<i>300 batches of kimchi.</i>

890
00:50:35,387 --> 00:50:37,055
<i>That's why I got…</i>

891
00:50:37,138 --> 00:50:38,640
You're shaking like crazy!

892
00:50:40,058 --> 00:50:42,227
You don't even have in-laws.
Why are you watching that?

893
00:50:42,310 --> 00:50:43,812
-Don't you know her?
-I don't.

894
00:50:43,895 --> 00:50:45,146
She's really popular.

895
00:50:45,230 --> 00:50:47,065
-Who is it?
-"Damn in-laws!"

896
00:50:48,358 --> 00:50:50,819
-She has over a million subscribers.
<i>-Damn in-laws!</i>

897
00:50:53,363 --> 00:50:54,990
That voice sounds familiar.

898
00:50:56,616 --> 00:50:57,826
"Damn in-laws"?

899
00:51:01,204 --> 00:51:04,332
Oh no. You caught me.

900
00:51:07,460 --> 00:51:10,046
This isn't going to be an exposé video.

901
00:51:10,130 --> 00:51:12,674
It's going to be a marketing video
for a luxury kindergarten.

902
00:51:12,757 --> 00:51:16,344
So keep the tone as luxurious
as you can, okay?

903
00:51:18,179 --> 00:51:20,807
Ms. Kang, begin when I give the sign.

904
00:51:21,725 --> 00:51:23,018
Don't worry.

905
00:51:23,101 --> 00:51:25,103
All right. Are you all ready?

906
00:51:31,693 --> 00:51:33,445
Let's go.

907
00:51:33,528 --> 00:51:34,571
Go on.

908
00:51:36,531 --> 00:51:39,534
Everyone, Taesan Construction
has introduced a special system

909
00:51:39,618 --> 00:51:41,578
to improve children's balance.

910
00:51:41,661 --> 00:51:44,748
An automatic floor-tilting system.

911
00:51:47,167 --> 00:51:49,461
When you place an apple on a table…

912
00:51:57,093 --> 00:52:00,055
As you can see,
they've installed this to help children

913
00:52:00,138 --> 00:52:01,306
build lower-body strength.

914
00:52:02,390 --> 00:52:04,976
Oh my. It seems like Taesan Construction

915
00:52:05,060 --> 00:52:07,562
wants to turn our kids
into future gymnastics champions.

916
00:52:10,482 --> 00:52:11,399
Oh, that's cold!

917
00:52:13,443 --> 00:52:16,196
You must be worried about
your children's skin in the dry winter.

918
00:52:16,279 --> 00:52:19,658
But here, there's a mist of cement dust
operating 24 hours a day.

919
00:52:19,741 --> 00:52:22,243
The damp atmosphere
gives off a high-end basement vibe.

920
00:52:22,327 --> 00:52:25,121
You could film <i>Parasite</i> here!

921
00:52:25,789 --> 00:52:26,706
How damp!

922
00:52:29,292 --> 00:52:32,921
Look at these luxurious drops of water
falling from the ceiling.

923
00:52:33,004 --> 00:52:35,256
Taesan Construction staff,

924
00:52:35,340 --> 00:52:38,259
would you like to come here
in person for a shower?

925
00:52:38,343 --> 00:52:39,177
Oh, that's cold!

926
00:52:39,260 --> 00:52:40,178
No way!

927
00:52:41,513 --> 00:52:43,014
And here's the highlight.

928
00:52:43,098 --> 00:52:46,351
Shall we see what they've hidden
behind this pretty facade

929
00:52:46,434 --> 00:52:49,187
saying "Enrollment Open"?

930
00:52:49,270 --> 00:52:51,189
Mothers, please reveal it!

931
00:52:55,443 --> 00:52:57,070
This is nuts.

932
00:52:58,446 --> 00:53:00,991
It seems they've made art
instead of a building.

933
00:53:01,074 --> 00:53:04,202
This premium crack pattern
is quite unique, isn't it?

934
00:53:04,953 --> 00:53:07,831
That's truly a magnificent crack.

935
00:53:07,914 --> 00:53:09,624
Subscribers,

936
00:53:09,708 --> 00:53:13,461
wouldn't it be a waste
to keep such a place to ourselves?

937
00:53:14,546 --> 00:53:17,632
So we'll share this secret with you all.

938
00:53:17,716 --> 00:53:19,467
Shoddy construction, zero conscience.

939
00:53:19,551 --> 00:53:20,719
The company name is…

940
00:53:21,636 --> 00:53:23,013
-Tae.
-San.

941
00:53:23,096 --> 00:53:24,848
-Con.
-Struction.

942
00:53:24,931 --> 00:53:25,890
No way!

943
00:53:26,933 --> 00:53:29,644
Damn in-laws.

944
00:53:29,728 --> 00:53:32,814
I might put up with in-laws,
but I won't put up with anyone

945
00:53:32,897 --> 00:53:34,315
harming our kids!

946
00:53:36,568 --> 00:53:38,236
<i>Listen up, Taesan Construction.</i>

947
00:53:38,778 --> 00:53:41,698
<i>We're getting back every penny</i>
<i>you skimmed from the rebar costs,</i>

948
00:53:41,781 --> 00:53:44,075
<i>so go ahead</i>
<i>and try holding out until the end.</i>

949
00:53:44,159 --> 00:53:46,327
Taesan Construction may silence the media,

950
00:53:46,411 --> 00:53:49,039
but they can't silence
my channel's subscribers.

951
00:53:49,122 --> 00:53:51,332
Should I upload the video now?

952
00:53:51,416 --> 00:53:52,917
Instead of fighting your in-laws,

953
00:53:53,001 --> 00:53:56,671
let's take on the construction company
for our children this time.

954
00:53:57,505 --> 00:53:59,007
All right, let's do this.

955
00:54:16,816 --> 00:54:18,610
Boss, look at the view count going up.

956
00:54:18,693 --> 00:54:19,736
It's insane.

957
00:54:19,819 --> 00:54:23,823
Why didn't I know that Seo-jun's mom
was "Damn In-Laws"?

958
00:54:23,907 --> 00:54:25,241
I'm a subscriber.

959
00:54:25,325 --> 00:54:27,368
"Is their headquarters
built out of Styrofoam?"

960
00:54:27,452 --> 00:54:28,953
"Taesan loves shoddy construction."

961
00:54:29,037 --> 00:54:30,413
The comments are blowing up.

962
00:54:31,372 --> 00:54:34,167
They were fools
to mess with Korean mothers.

963
00:54:34,250 --> 00:54:37,337
They may silence the media,
but they can't silence the mothers.

964
00:54:37,420 --> 00:54:38,254
Right.

965
00:54:38,338 --> 00:54:40,465
Taesan Construction
should be responding soon.

966
00:54:41,049 --> 00:54:41,883
Of course.

967
00:54:42,884 --> 00:54:46,721
We're contacting influencers
who are spreading the video

968
00:54:46,805 --> 00:54:48,264
and asking them to delete it.

969
00:54:48,848 --> 00:54:51,935
Most of them did
when we offered money, but…

970
00:54:52,018 --> 00:54:53,520
"But"?

971
00:54:54,687 --> 00:54:57,357
There are posts on
the True Value mothers' online community

972
00:54:57,440 --> 00:54:59,150
requesting an explanation from Taesan

973
00:54:59,234 --> 00:55:03,446
and a full safety inspection
of the apartment complex.

974
00:55:04,114 --> 00:55:06,699
What the hell is the legal team doing?

975
00:55:07,450 --> 00:55:10,578
Mothers' community or not,
just sue everyone.

976
00:55:10,662 --> 00:55:13,540
Make sure everyone who spreads the video

977
00:55:13,623 --> 00:55:16,459
will want to cut off their own hands.

978
00:55:17,043 --> 00:55:18,795
Yes, sir.

979
00:55:22,090 --> 00:55:23,883
SENIOR SECRETARY SONG U-SIK

980
00:55:24,551 --> 00:55:25,760
What about the old geezers?

981
00:55:29,472 --> 00:55:31,015
The Prosecutor General

982
00:55:31,099 --> 00:55:34,144
seems to be contacting
other construction company presidents.

983
00:55:35,520 --> 00:55:36,354
What?

984
00:55:37,230 --> 00:55:38,898
How dare he?

985
00:55:38,982 --> 00:55:42,610
It seems like he's trying to find
a company to keep Taesan in check.

986
00:55:43,194 --> 00:55:44,654
Keep Taesan in check?

987
00:55:47,031 --> 00:55:50,160
Who do they think they are
to keep me in check?

988
00:55:50,243 --> 00:55:54,122
They're all just sitting around
waiting for me to bring them money.

989
00:55:56,374 --> 00:55:57,625
GONGYEONG DAILY LEE SANG-GYU

990
00:55:57,709 --> 00:56:00,044
These old geezers are all panicking,

991
00:56:00,837 --> 00:56:04,757
worried this will affect
the Oman New Town project.

992
00:56:05,800 --> 00:56:06,801
Park Hae-kang…

993
00:56:07,677 --> 00:56:08,970
Park Hae-kang!

994
00:56:11,097 --> 00:56:12,724
I loved his competence,

995
00:56:13,808 --> 00:56:15,393
but now that he's my enemy,

996
00:56:16,144 --> 00:56:17,562
I want to kill him.

997
00:56:21,274 --> 00:56:23,234
Not a single person is passing by.

998
00:56:23,318 --> 00:56:26,654
Why do we have to sit out here
in the freezing cold?

999
00:56:26,738 --> 00:56:29,866
The boss told us to make sure
nobody goes inside.

1000
00:56:29,949 --> 00:56:32,202
They'll come to get rid of the evidence.

1001
00:56:32,285 --> 00:56:34,245
I put up thermal sensors
all around the entrance.

1002
00:56:34,329 --> 00:56:36,164
The alarm will go off
even if an ant walks by.

1003
00:56:36,247 --> 00:56:38,708
But don't the Taesan guys sleep at all?

1004
00:56:38,791 --> 00:56:41,711
They'd have to be paid
for night shifts too.

1005
00:56:41,794 --> 00:56:42,837
Don't be stupid.

1006
00:56:42,921 --> 00:56:45,632
Would thieves even care about labor laws?

1007
00:56:45,715 --> 00:56:46,841
Geez.

1008
00:56:47,508 --> 00:56:48,801
Intruder alert!

1009
00:56:49,427 --> 00:56:50,762
Cover me!

1010
00:57:02,190 --> 00:57:03,024
Damn it.

1011
00:57:03,566 --> 00:57:06,152
Is this a secret weapon sent by Taesan?

1012
00:57:06,236 --> 00:57:07,987
Sorry, that's the snack I was eating.

1013
00:57:08,780 --> 00:57:10,740
Just pick one. Doze off or eat.

1014
00:57:10,823 --> 00:57:12,075
Intruder alert canceled.

1015
00:57:13,326 --> 00:57:15,536
Good job. Stick to the manual.

1016
00:57:15,620 --> 00:57:16,913
Manual, my foot…

1017
00:57:31,469 --> 00:57:32,929
This is so satisfying.

1018
00:57:33,012 --> 00:57:35,765
We need to have <i>japchae</i> to celebrate.

1019
00:57:35,848 --> 00:57:36,766
Boss, look at this.

1020
00:57:36,849 --> 00:57:39,269
Our community forum
is blowing up right now.

1021
00:57:39,352 --> 00:57:41,396
Lee Chung-won's going
to feel pressured for sure.

1022
00:57:41,479 --> 00:57:42,647
Right.

1023
00:57:43,982 --> 00:57:46,109
He still pisses me off, though.
How dare he?

1024
00:57:46,192 --> 00:57:48,945
If he lays a finger on our old boss,

1025
00:57:49,028 --> 00:57:51,990
I'm going to tear
the whole Oman New Town apart.

1026
00:57:53,324 --> 00:57:55,368
You shouldn't slice the carrots like that!

1027
00:57:55,451 --> 00:57:56,661
This is for the <i>japchae</i>.

1028
00:57:56,744 --> 00:57:58,496
The sizes are all different.

1029
00:57:58,580 --> 00:57:59,872
Is this for Gyeong-buk?

1030
00:57:59,956 --> 00:58:02,083
Why are you cutting them
into whale shapes?

1031
00:58:02,166 --> 00:58:05,295
Je-gil, you should be helping me out here.

1032
00:58:05,378 --> 00:58:06,838
You're just staring at that forum.

1033
00:58:06,921 --> 00:58:09,173
I should just destroy that laptop.

1034
00:58:09,257 --> 00:58:11,426
-Look at him.
-Wait, Boss.

1035
00:58:11,509 --> 00:58:13,303
I think you should see this.

1036
00:58:15,096 --> 00:58:16,347
Mr. Park.

1037
00:58:16,431 --> 00:58:18,683
That post on the forum…

1038
00:58:18,766 --> 00:58:20,518
What's going on?

1039
00:58:22,854 --> 00:58:24,689
EXPOSING PARK HAE-KANG'S CORRUPTION

1040
00:58:30,486 --> 00:58:33,031
I'm the facility manager
of True Value State,

1041
00:58:34,198 --> 00:58:35,908
Choi Yeong-jae.

1042
00:58:36,492 --> 00:58:37,410
<i>Today,</i>

1043
00:58:38,703 --> 00:58:41,289
<i>I am staking</i>
<i>my lifelong professional integrity</i>

1044
00:58:41,914 --> 00:58:43,708
<i>on the truth I'm about to reveal.</i>

1045
00:58:44,709 --> 00:58:47,629
The 17.8 billion won
in the long-term repair reserve fund

1046
00:58:47,712 --> 00:58:50,256
that all the residents
gathered over the past years…

1047
00:58:52,675 --> 00:58:54,427
was embezzled by President Park Hae-kang

1048
00:58:56,471 --> 00:58:58,931
and the accounting manager, Kang Ha-jeong,

1049
00:59:00,224 --> 00:59:01,267
as part

1050
00:59:02,727 --> 00:59:03,936
of an organized scheme.

1051
00:59:04,729 --> 00:59:06,648
<i>I am ashamed to admit</i>

1052
00:59:07,273 --> 00:59:10,193
<i>that as the facility manager,</i>
<i>I was deceived and used by them,</i>

1053
00:59:10,276 --> 00:59:11,903
<i>blinded by their elaborate collusion</i>

1054
00:59:12,737 --> 00:59:14,030
<i>and falsified documents.</i>

1055
00:59:14,113 --> 00:59:17,241
What kind of bullshit is this?

1056
00:59:18,284 --> 00:59:20,119
<i>It's late,</i>
<i>but I found the courage to confess</i>

1057
00:59:20,703 --> 00:59:22,705
<i>in order to prevent any further harm.</i>

1058
00:59:22,789 --> 00:59:24,916
<i>President Park embezzled the reserve fund.</i>

1059
00:59:25,958 --> 00:59:27,168
Goodness.

1060
00:59:27,251 --> 00:59:28,961
What? Embezzled?

1061
00:59:29,045 --> 00:59:30,088
Oh my goodness.

1062
00:59:30,171 --> 00:59:31,714
<i>They embezzled how much?</i>

1063
00:59:31,798 --> 00:59:33,716
<i>It's 17.8 billion won!</i>

1064
00:59:34,676 --> 00:59:36,469
No way! 17.8 billion?

1065
00:59:38,304 --> 00:59:39,931
They embezzled 17.8 billion?

1066
00:59:40,848 --> 00:59:43,976
This doesn't even compare
to President Seo.

1067
00:59:44,852 --> 00:59:46,479
<i>I promise to cooperate</i>

1068
00:59:47,980 --> 00:59:49,899
<i>with any investigations.</i>

1069
00:59:50,608 --> 00:59:51,984
You still can't reach Mr. Choi?

1070
00:59:52,068 --> 00:59:53,069
<i>The number you've dialed…</i>

1071
00:59:53,152 --> 00:59:55,238
His phone's turned off.

1072
00:59:55,321 --> 00:59:57,198
Should we just unplug all the phones?

1073
00:59:57,281 --> 00:59:58,783
<i>Lastly,</i>

1074
00:59:58,866 --> 01:00:02,286
<i>I sincerely apologize to all the residents</i>

1075
01:00:03,663 --> 01:00:04,956
<i>of True Value.</i>

1076
01:00:16,259 --> 01:00:17,969
I can't believe this.

1077
01:00:18,052 --> 01:00:21,055
He's claiming that Mr. Park
and Ha-jeong took the 17.8 billion?

1078
01:00:21,139 --> 01:00:23,057
Why is this happening?

1079
01:00:23,141 --> 01:00:24,183
This is ridiculous.

1080
01:00:24,267 --> 01:00:25,893
Mr. Choi is stabbing us in the back

1081
01:00:25,977 --> 01:00:27,603
when he's the one who took the money.

1082
01:00:28,354 --> 01:00:29,313
Boss.

1083
01:00:30,398 --> 01:00:31,232
What do we do?

1084
01:00:31,983 --> 01:00:34,068
-Boss!
-What should we do?

1085
01:00:34,694 --> 01:00:35,737
Who is it this time?

1086
01:00:35,820 --> 01:00:36,988
Tell them to come back later.

1087
01:00:38,156 --> 01:00:39,741
<i>Police! Open the door.</i>

1088
01:00:41,492 --> 01:00:42,452
-Pol…
-Police?

1089
01:00:42,535 --> 01:00:43,828
How did they come so quickly?

1090
01:00:43,911 --> 01:00:45,997
I'll go and buy some time.

1091
01:00:46,080 --> 01:00:47,707
-No, wait!
-Why?

1092
01:00:47,790 --> 01:00:50,001
Don't open the door just yet.

1093
01:00:50,752 --> 01:00:53,087
What do we do now, Mr. Park?

1094
01:00:53,755 --> 01:00:55,673
Lizard, Ha-jeong, get inside.

1095
01:00:57,341 --> 01:00:58,509
You guys hide too.

1096
01:00:58,593 --> 01:01:00,052
-Ms. Kang, come on.
-Hurry up!

1097
01:01:00,136 --> 01:01:01,596
What are we supposed to do?

1098
01:01:02,096 --> 01:01:03,723
-Hurry up.
-Go inside.

1099
01:01:14,275 --> 01:01:16,903
Sangwon Police Major Crimes Unit.
Mr. Park Hae-kang?

1100
01:01:17,487 --> 01:01:19,363
You're under arrest

1101
01:01:19,447 --> 01:01:21,073
for embezzlement and breach of trust.

1102
01:01:21,157 --> 01:01:24,786
Due to the risk of flight,
we're arresting you without a warrant.

1103
01:01:24,869 --> 01:01:27,205
You have the right to retain an attorney,

1104
01:01:27,288 --> 01:01:29,707
to present your defense,
and to remain silent.

1105
01:01:29,791 --> 01:01:32,084
Anything you say can
and will be used against you--

1106
01:01:32,168 --> 01:01:33,044
Let's go.

1107
01:01:34,754 --> 01:01:35,588
Boss!

1108
01:01:35,671 --> 01:01:37,507
Let go!

1109
01:01:37,590 --> 01:01:39,175
-Don't touch the officer.
-Step back!

1110
01:01:39,258 --> 01:01:40,843
-Hey.
-Wait!

1111
01:01:42,261 --> 01:01:44,055
You should explain what's going on!

1112
01:01:44,138 --> 01:01:44,972
Boss.

1113
01:01:45,056 --> 01:01:46,808
The facility manager was lying!

1114
01:01:46,891 --> 01:01:48,559
-Boss.
-Boss.

1115
01:01:49,143 --> 01:01:50,102
Mr. Park.

1116
01:02:03,032 --> 01:02:05,451
THE APARTMENT JOB

1117
01:02:29,559 --> 01:02:32,979
How can this be the face of someone
who took 17.8 billion won?

1118
01:02:33,062 --> 01:02:34,438
Let me talk to you, Mr. Choi.

1119
01:02:34,522 --> 01:02:35,815
What's with you?

1120
01:02:37,483 --> 01:02:38,901
Get him!

1121
01:02:38,985 --> 01:02:41,737
<i>I'm actually curious.</i>

1122
01:02:41,821 --> 01:02:43,030
<i>Did you really think</i>

1123
01:02:43,114 --> 01:02:46,200
<i>exposing that shoddy construction</i>
<i>would achieve some great justice?</i>

1124
01:02:46,868 --> 01:02:48,202
Your photos look great.

1125
01:02:48,286 --> 01:02:50,204
<i>We should be sticking together.</i>

1126
01:02:50,288 --> 01:02:52,248
<i>Stick together and do what?</i>

1127
01:02:52,331 --> 01:02:54,166
<i>We have to stay right here, as a family.</i>

1128
01:02:54,250 --> 01:02:55,501
You thief!

1129
01:02:56,377 --> 01:02:57,461
I won't run away

1130
01:02:57,545 --> 01:03:00,339
<i>until we catch the one</i>
<i>who took the 17.8 billion.</i>

1131
01:03:00,423 --> 01:03:01,674
It was my oversight.

1132
01:03:01,757 --> 01:03:04,343
<i>We will rebuild it</i>
<i>into one of the finest kindergartens.</i>

1133
01:03:04,427 --> 01:03:05,469
<i>President Lee Chung-won.</i>

1134
01:03:05,553 --> 01:03:08,556
<i>Are you going to demolish all 9,800</i>
<i>apartments here and rebuild them again?</i>

1135
01:03:08,639 --> 01:03:11,267
<i>He's really blowing everything up.</i>

1136
01:03:14,854 --> 01:03:16,856
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

